course: dictionary
lesson: 13733
title: Words that grow stronger
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words show change, and «intensified» is one of them. It is the past tense of intensify, which means to make something stronger, bigger or more extreme. When you meet intensified, ask: did something become stronger by itself, or did someone make it stronger on purpose?
explain: «The storm intensified overnight.» Nobody chose this. The wind and rain grew stronger on their own, so intensified means became stronger. Now read «The police intensified their search.» This time the police decided to make their search stronger, so intensified can also mean made stronger on purpose.
explain: Use a check. Swap in a phrase such as grew stronger or stepped up. If «The storm stepped up overnight» sounds odd, the first meaning fits. If «The police stepped up their search» makes sense, the second meaning is right.
fact: Intensify means to make something stronger, or to become stronger.
fact: «Intensified» is the past tense of intensify, so it tells us that something already happened.
fact: «The storm intensified» means the storm became stronger on its own.
fact: «Intensified efforts» means people worked harder on purpose.
fact: Synonyms for intensified include grew stronger, increased and stepped up.
exercise: «The storm intensified overnight.» What does intensified mean here? | Stopped completely | Moved to the next town | Became smaller and quieter | *Became stronger
exercise: «The police intensified their search.» What does intensified mean here? | Kept the search exactly the same | Stopped the search | Forgot where they had already looked | *Made their search stronger on purpose
exercise: «The fighting intensified during the night.» Which word could replace intensified? | *grew stronger | went home | grew calmer | was forgotten
test: «The coach intensified the training before the big match.» Why did the coach do this? | To check the weather | *To make the training stronger on purpose | To stop the team from training | To cancel the match
test: «As the sun rose, the heat intensified.» Which word means the same as intensified here? | Cooled | Paused | *Increased | Vanished
exam: Mia writes, «The noise intensified.» Did the noise get quieter or stronger? | Later | *Stronger | Quieter | Shorter
